    "summary": "No single deterministic hash function $h: \\mathcal{U} \\to \\{0, 1, \\dots, m-1\\}$ can perform well on all inputs: by the Pigeonhole Principle , whenever the universe size $|\\mathcal{U}| \\ge N \\cdot m + 1$, there exists a s",
