        "title": "Step 3: Implement evaluate()",
        "concept": "Dietzfelbinger's Multiply-Shift hashing (a·k >> (64-r) with random odd a) achieves 2/m collision bounds in 3 C...",
        "instructions": "Complete `evaluate(uint64_t x)` in `src/main.cpp` by replacing `TODO (Step 3)` with the algorithm logic.",
        "hint": "x = modMersenne(x);\nuint64_t acc = coeff_[K - 1];\nfor (size_t i = K - 1; i-- > 0; ) {\nacc = modMersenne(static_cast<__uint128_t>(acc) * x + coeff_[i]);",
