    "summary": "Searching for the same query key $q$ across $k$ separate sorted lists of length $n$ naively costs $O(k \\log n)$ time. Fractional Cascading (Chazelle & Guibas, 1986) bubbles every second element of list $L_{i+1}$ upward i",
